# As-received checksums for the starter kit's protected files.
#
# The assignment says: "Don't change the ticketing API itself; if you have to, say
# what you changed and why in your README." The mock is the fixture — the whole
# exercise is surviving its failures, so editing it would invalidate the work.
#
# These hashes were recorded at Stage 0, from the files exactly as received in the
# starter kit. Nothing in the mock has been edited: the kit's files were moved to
# the repository root (mock-ticketing/, CONTRACT.md) and to this folder
# (README.md, cases.sample.json), and their contents were not touched.
#
# tests/unit/test_starter_kit_integrity.py recomputes these on every test run, so
# an accidental edit to the fixture fails the suite rather than quietly changing
# the thing being measured.
#
# Format is the standard sha256sum layout: <64 hex chars><two spaces><relative path>
#
# Deliberately not listed:
#   docker-compose.yml  — ours to extend (it gains the agent, MCP and web services)
#   README.md, cases.sample.json — kept here for provenance; sample input and
#                        documentation, not part of the fixture's contract
